§ 15 M₂ METRIC SPECIFICATION
  version   = v1.1.0 ← introduced post-v1.0, ADDITIVE
  stable?   = ◐ experimental → stable on-acceptance (Apocky-confirm)
  owner     = scripts/compute_m2.py + friends
  related   = §10 EVAL (m₁ stratification precedent)

§ I> PURPOSE
  empirical validation of-the density=sovereignty claim
  ← m₁ measures bytes-on-disk ← m₂ measures bits-per-token under LLM

§§ DEFINITION ← formal
  m₂ ≡ ⟦ mean-NLL(CSL) / mean-NLL(EN-paraphrase) ⟧
  where :
    NLL(seq, model) = -Σᵢ log P(tokenᵢ | token<ᵢ ; model)
    mean-NLL(seq, model) = NLL / |tokens(seq)|
  units : dimensionless ratio

§§ INTERPRETATION ← reading-the-numbers
  m₂ < 1.0   ← CSL more-predictable-than-EN
               ∴ unlikely (rare-glyphs weigh against CSL)
  m₂ ≈ 1.0   ← equal-density (CSL = EN in-nats-per-token)
  m₂ ≤ 1.2   ← target ← CSL ≤ 1.2× EN-perplexity
  m₂ > 1.5   ← CSL too-surprising ← model unfamiliar-with-notation
  m₂ > 2.0   ← likely-failure of-density-claim ← investigate

§§ CAVEAT ← non-identity of-measurement-with-claim
  PPL measures model-familiarity AS-WELL-AS density
  ∴ pre-trained models have-EN-bias ⇒ m₂ ≥ 1.0 expected
  ∴ m₂ measures relative-density ¬ absolute-quality
  ∴ multi-model evaluation reduces single-model-bias
  ∴ fine-tuned CSL-aware model would-yield lower-m₂ ← separate-experiment

§§ STRATIFIED TARGETS ← per-mode ← matches §10-m₁-stratification
  | mode      | m₂-target | rationale                                    |
  |-----------|-----------|----------------------------------------------|
  | pure-CSL  | ≤ 1.5     | dense-glyphs unfamiliar to-general-LLMs     |
  | bridge    | ≤ 1.2     | mixed EN+CSL ← LLM-friendly                 |
  | prose     | ≤ 1.05    | mostly-EN ← near-baseline expected          |

§§ PROTOCOL ← reproducibility
  W! temperature = 0
  W! sampling = deterministic (no random-sample)
  W! seed = fixed-constant (default 20260417)
  W! tokenizer = model-native (¬ custom)
  W! NLL-aggregation = arithmetic-mean per-token
  W! model-weight-SHA pinned-per-run
  W! paraphrase-SHA captured-in-audit-chain
  W! multi-model ≥ 3 models different-families

§§ MODEL SET ← initial-corpus
  small  : Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M       ~ 0.9 GB
  medium : Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M       ~ 1.9 GB
  large  : Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3-Q4_K_M    ~ 4.1 GB
  total  : ≤ 8 GB disk-budget
  rationale :
    ✓ 3-models = inter-model variance signal
    ✓ different families = reduce single-arch bias
    ✓ Q4_K_M = quality-vs-size tradeoff
    ✓ all permissively-licensed
    ✓ GGUF available ← llama.cpp compatible

§§ BOOTSTRAP CI ← non-parametric
  method : percentile-bootstrap
  resamples : 1000 default
  confidence : 95% two-sided
  formula : CI = (q₀.₀₂₅, q₀.₉₇₅) of-resampled-m₂-distribution

§§ PARAPHRASE QUALITY ← gating
  methodology :
    1 embedding-cosine via sentence-transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2
    2 entity-recall via identifier-extraction + stemming
  thresholds :
    | backend                | cosine | recall |
    |------------------------|--------|--------|
    | sentence-transformers  | 0.70   | 0.80   |
    | char-5-gram-jaccard    | 0.03   | 0.15   |
  fallback-rationale : Jaccard is-gross-mismatch-gate only
  flagged-pairs : require Apocky-review + CHANGELOG-entry

§§ AUDIT CHAIN ← R16-anchor
  location : .m2-chain/runs.jsonl
  keys     : .m2-chain/keys/{private,public}.key (32-byte Ed25519 raw)
  entry-fields :
    seq prev_hash run_id timestamp
    file file_hash paraphrase paraphrase_hash
    model_key model_name model_hash
    m2_value m2_ci_low m2_ci_high seed backend signature
  canonical-form = pipe-joined fields ← signed-via-Ed25519
  verify-cmd : python scripts/m2_audit.py --verify

§§ CACHE ← incremental
  key : BLAKE3(file-content + paraphrase-content + model-hash + algo-version)
  value : (m₂, CI, per-token-NLL, timestamp)
  location : .m2-cache/
  invalidation : natural hash-mismatch on-any-change

§§ COMPARISON HARNESS ← notation-context
  reference-content : 5 short-passages (algorithm descriptions)
  notations : CSL • APL • Lojban • prose
  metrics : char-count • token-count • mean-NLL • compression-vs-prose
  caveat ‼ : APL + Lojban high-NLL ≡ LLM-unfamiliarity ¬ anti-density
  use : density-ordering ← informational ¬ authoritative

§§ FILES
  scripts/compute_m2.py         ← core harness
  scripts/m2_models.py          ← model registry + SHA-pinning
  scripts/m2_install_models.sh  ← bootstrap downloader
  scripts/m2_quality.py         ← paraphrase-quality scorer
  scripts/m2_audit.py           ← Ed25519 chain
  scripts/m2_visualize.py       ← HTML heatmap reporter
  scripts/m2_compare.py         ← CSL vs APL vs Lojban vs prose
  eval/paraphrases/C{1..7}.en   ← plain-text EN paraphrases
  eval/m2_baseline.json         ← recorded m₂-table
  eval/m2_quality.json          ← paraphrase-quality snapshot
  eval/m2_results/              ← per-run artifacts
  benchmarks/m2_throughput.md   ← perf table
  benchmarks/m2_comparison.md   ← notation comparison results
  diag/M2_INTERPRETATION.md     ← how-to-read caveats
  specs/15_M2_METRIC.csl        ← this-file

§§ ACCEPTANCE ← Session-11-exit
  ✓ 3 models installed + SHA-verified
  ✓ 7 EN paraphrases written + Apocky-reviewed
  ✓ paraphrase-quality scores ≥ thresholds
  ✓ m₂ computed ∀ (file × model) = 21 measurements
  ✓ bootstrap-CI reported per-measurement
  ✓ stratified-targets met OR deviation documented
  ✓ HTML visualization produced
  ✓ comparison-harness output (CSL < prose)
  ✓ audit-chain verifies clean
  ✓ cache hit-on-second-run < 100ms

§§ CHANGES-POLICY ← post-v1.0
  ADDITIVE-ONLY : ← STABILITY.md commitment
    add new fields to JSON outputs ← allowed (MINOR)
    add new CLI flags ← allowed (MINOR)
    remove-or-rename existing surface ← MAJOR
    change threshold numerics ← MINOR (with-CHANGELOG-note)
    replace metric-algorithm ← MAJOR

§§ OPEN-QUESTIONS ← Session-12+
  Q? fine-tune a model on CSL-corpus ← measure Δm₂
     (expected : m₂ decreases substantially post-fine-tune)
  Q? per-glyph NLL breakdown ← which glyphs are-BPE-costly
     (feeds back into-§12 tokenizer decision-procedure)
  Q? Zipf-law analysis over-glyph-frequency ← is-CSL Zipfian?
  Q? cross-linguistic : compare m₂ across En / Zh / Ja
     model-tokenizer-family bias

∎ SPEC 15
